{
  "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
  "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:22 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents in this case have for years benefited enormously from their free and exclusive use of public spectrum. They argue, however, that neither Congress nor the commission may as a condition of their licenses require that they refrain from broadcasting indecent material when children are most likely to be in the audience."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, General Verrilli, it seems to me that this contract notion of yours can only go so far. I mean, if the idea is just we gave them something, now they have to do whatever we say, you wouldn't accept that. So, the question is why is this condition appropriate when many other conditions would not be appropriate? I mean, tell me if I'm wrong, if you would say all conditions are appropriate. But I -- I frankly think you wouldn't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's one of their arguments. I mean, another one is that you haven't defined it precisely enough, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Verrilli",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The V-chip works with both broadcast and -- and cable transmissions, to the extent it works."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Verrilli",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "does a very thorough job in explaining the many ways in which the V-chip has proven to be a deficient technology."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Fox Television Stations, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, why not just keep it as it is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that there is a difference between what a person sees on broadcast channels and what a person sees on basic cable? Basic cable now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What you acknowledge to be the vulgarity of cable suggests otherwise, doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: When the issue is the content-based regulation of speech, it is the government, not the speaker, that must steer, quote, \"far wide of the prohibited zone.\" That foundational principle is nowhere in evidence in the FCC's current enforcement regime, which not only intrudes into the prohibited zone but also enforces the indecency ban in a starkly inconsistent manner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How many displays -- how many displays of nudity were there that -- that went unsanctioned?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, we -- well, we have to anticipate what the natural results or consequences of our decision will be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-1293",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05c87c8b8ec8c2045ccac9714ff48af99e9cffe10afc61bebd90171751f98b06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05c87c8b8ec8-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
